#40101
A Spacious Cloak Room~
   Stretching along the southern wall of the great hallway you pass into is a
coat rack, from which hang dozens of cloaks, furs, capes and large satchels,
containing the worthless junk accumulated by these brutish giants in their
travels.  Any items of worth are doubtless by now sequestered elsewhere, a
search here would be pointless.  The wall to the north is lined with doors,
three to be precise, spaced evenly along the wall as it heads west.  Peering
into the gloom, you see only sporadic lighting, cast by sputtering tar-soaked
torches.    
~
